.md
## Faster I/O
Multi step refactor over the whole codebase of WLJS Notebook opened up the opportunity to tighten and factor out frontend - backend API. We no longer evaluate an arbitrary expressions on the backend, only a limited set of optocodes and non-executable payload is allowed. Javascript $\\rightarrow$ WL pipeline now relies on binary protocol with an efificent WXF serializer implementation with zero-copy approach for typed arrays and binary payload. All together:

- __x2__ <abbr title="it was always fast actually">faster</abbr> Kernel (WL) $\\rightarrow$ Frontend (Javascript)
- __x7400__ faster Frontend (Javascript) $\\rightarrow$ Kernel (WL)

You can literally stream raw uncompressed vide in real-time to the backend using something like this:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
