.md
## Faster initial launch, faster package loading
It turned out, that out autocomplete feature based around `$NewSymbol` expression, which is called on every symbol allocation was causing noticeable kernel lag as well as silent context switching (the trickest bug we've ever faced). We no longer use it, but rather periodically scan contextes using safer approch - `Names[]`. __This sped up the initial launch by the factor of x8__.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Faster initial launch, faster package loading
It turned out, that out autocomplete feature based around `$NewSymbol` expression, which is called on every symbol allocation was causing noticeable kernel lag as well as silent context switching (the trickest bug we've ever faced). We no longer use it, but rather periodically scan contextes using safer approch - `Names[]`. __This sped up the initial launch by the factor of x8__.

