## Improved Mathematica notebooks import
Here we should be honest with you. Originally the converting process was hardcoded for certain cell types and expressions, which was very fragile. The major issue is that Mathematica has many typesetting expressions, which are not documented, and they are mixed with textual constructions. Some are nice and can be mapped 1:1 to WLJS, while others requires TeX forms to really look readable. At this point we utilized for the first time in this project an AI assistance. Though multiple iterations it was refined to the point when 10 random notebooks found on the internet and in our closet could be opened and rendered correctly.

